<DocsLayout
  title="Loops"
  subtitle="Server-side, headless Loops engine: a thin orchestrator that composes Scheduler + Goal. Source: packages/nikcli/src/loop/."
  description="Guide to Nikcli’s headless loop engine, scheduled workflows, stages, triggers, and orchestration events."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="overview" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      A <strong>Loop</strong> is a named, persisted workflow that runs an ordered list of
      <strong>stages</strong>, each of which is a single <code>goal</code> command executed by a
      worker agent. A <strong>trigger</strong> — manual or interval — decides when the loop fires.
    </p>
    <p>
      The headless <code>LoopEngine</code> (<code>packages/nikcli/src/loop/engine.ts</code>) owns the
      interval timers via the core <code>Scheduler</code> with <code>scope: "instance"</code>, so
      scheduled loops keep firing when the TUI is closed. The TUI feature plugin
      (<code>packages/nikcli/src/cli/cmd/tui/feature-plugins/loops/</code>) is a thin client over
      the SDK: it subscribes to bus events for live status, and uses the SDK to create, run, pause,
      resume, and delete loops.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-8">
      <DocCard title="Composition over reinvention" eyebrow="Primitives">
        <p>
          A Loop does not reimplement iteration, budgets, or autonomy. The interval trigger is a
          <code>Scheduler.register</code> call; each run is a <code>SessionPrompt.command</code>
          invocation of <code>goal</code>. The existing <code>Goal</code> engine does the rest.
        </p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Headless by design" eyebrow="No TUI required">
        <p>
          Definitions are persisted in <code>Storage</code>; timers live in the server process.
          Loops fire on schedule regardless of whether a TUI is connected. A TUI that connects
          later syncs the live state through bus events.
        </p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Crash-safe" eyebrow="Persistence">
        <p>
          A loop and its run history are persisted after every step. Stale <code>running</code> runs
          are reconciled to <code>orphaned</code> on the next boot by a lease/heartbeat
          (<code>LOOP_RUN_LEASE_MS = 15s</code>).
        </p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Concurrency cap" eyebrow="Back-pressure">
        <p>
          A global cap of <code>MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS = 3</code> prevents runaway workers. A
          per-loop single-flight claim prevents overlapping runs of the same loop.
        </p>
      </DocCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="concepts" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Concepts</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Definition</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Loop</strong></td><td>Named, persisted unit: a trigger, a list of stages, optional <code>maxRuns</code> and <code>timeoutMs</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Stage</strong></td><td>One unit of work within a run: name, agent, optional model, objective, optional token budget.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Trigger</strong></td><td><code>&#123; kind: "manual" &#125;</code> or <code>&#123; kind: "interval", everyMs &#125;</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Run</strong></td><td>A single execution of the loop's stages. Carries lease/heartbeat and a session id per stage.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Runtime</strong></td><td>Live, in-memory status of a loop (idle | running | paused | error | cancelling), updated by the engine on every bus event.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Template</strong></td><td>A named, parameterised loop draft the user can clone and customize.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="schema" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Loop schema</h2>
    <p>
      All persisted types live in <code>packages/nikcli/src/loop/schema.ts</code> as zod schemas.
    </p>
    <h3>Trigger</h3>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="packages/nikcli/src/loop/schema.ts">
export const LoopTriggerSchema = z.discriminatedUnion("kind", [
  z.object(&lbrace; kind: z.literal("manual") &rbrace;),
  z.object(&lbrace; kind: z.literal("interval"), everyMs: z.number().int().positive() &rbrace;),
])
    </DocCode>
